{
  "id": "kadison-kaplansky-projections",
  "title": "A torsion-free counterexample to the Kadison–Kaplansky conjecture",
  "description": "Kadison and Kaplansky conjectured that the reduced group C*-algebra of a torsion-free group contains no projections other than 0 and 1. OpenAI constructed in 2026 a finitely generated torsion-free group with a projection whose canonical trace lies strictly between 0 and 1/2. The group is defined by the closed walks of a voltage cover of an infinite layered expander, the tower, with voltages in a torsion-free nilpotent group; a weighted adjacency matrix over its group ring has a separated spectral band of small trace, and compression after a free product gives the scalar projection. The tower is built from streams and gated permutations and pruned so that long paths are recovered from their words; the voltages realize a model operator assembled from Schwartz idempotents of twisted group algebras, with one random draw per edge. The course is an exposition of OpenAI's proof (2026).",
